  "post_run_reflection": {
    "forbidden_near_neighbor_retry": "Do not retry by sweeping cash-conversion ratio, accruals/assets threshold, annual fact freshness, RS/close/volume/vol guards, top-N, hold days, cooldown, or notional on these frozen windows.",
    "new_evidence_required": "The positive-EV-but-drawdown-failing readout means the next valid test is a DIFFERENT decision hypothesis: a drawdown-aware deployment of this quality source (concurrent-position cap, per-name protective stop, or a risk-budgeted sub-sleeve) sized to the accepted comparators, or a sharper quality discriminator (PIT TTM same-period accruals, accrual-change momentum, or quarterly cash-flow when reported) that selects fewer, higher-conviction names. A drawdown-controlled redesign is not a threshold sweep of this rejected fixed bundle.",
    "outcome_summary": "Aggregate EV delta +0.9921; aggregate PnL delta $+21,322.65; max drawdown drift +0.0522; 369 paper trades.",
    "why_result_happened": "Rejected on drawdown drift only. The accruals / cash-conversion quality source was positively predictive: aggregate EV +0.9921 and PnL $+21,322.65 with positive EV/PnL in all three windows and no regression, beating the accepted compression and distribution comparators on the gross deltas, and concentration passed. The binding failure is that 369 paper trades (~1/day held 10 days, ~10 concurrent positions of momentum-confirmed quality names) form a large, highly-deployed sleeve whose drawdown drift (+0.0522) exceeds the 0.5pp guardrail. The gross-delta beat over the much smaller accepted comparators is partly a deployment-size artifact, not proven risk-adjusted superiority; 36/47 universe names pass the quality gate, so selection is discriminated mostly by price confirmation, i.e. the sleeve behaves like a broad cash-conversion-tilted momentum overlay."
  },
